
Here’s how you can implement an alarm-like notifier in Java for an Android app. This solution ensures the notification is snoozed every 5 minutes until the user interacts with it (clicks or dismisses):

---

### 1. **Set up Firebase Notifications**
Ensure Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) is integrated into your app. Refer to the [Firebase setup guide](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/android/client).

---

### 2. **Receive FCM Messages**
Use a `FirebaseMessagingService` to handle incoming FCM messages.

```java
public class MyFirebaseMessagingService extends FirebaseMessagingService {
    @Override
    public void onMessageReceived(@NonNull RemoteMessage remoteMessage) {
        if (remoteMessage.getNotification() != null) {
            showNotification(remoteMessage.getNotification().getTitle(), remoteMessage.getNotification().getBody());
        }
    }

    private void showNotification(String title, String message) {
        int notificationId = (int) System.currentTimeMillis();

        // Create Dismiss Intent
        Intent dismissIntent = new Intent(this, NotificationDismissReceiver.class);
        dismissIntent.setAction("DISMISS");
        dismissIntent.putExtra("NOTIFICATION_ID", notificationId);
        PendingIntent dismissPendingIntent = PendingIntent.getBroadcast(
                this,
                notificationId,
                dismissIntent,
                PendingIntent.FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT
        );

        // Create Notification
        NotificationCompat.Builder builder = new NotificationCompat.Builder(this, "default_channel")
                .setContentTitle(title)
                .setContentText(message)
                .setSmallIcon(R.drawable.ic_notification)
                .setAutoCancel(true)
                .addAction(R.drawable.ic_dismiss, "Dismiss", dismissPendingIntent);

        NotificationManagerCompat notificationManager = NotificationManagerCompat.from(this);
        notificationManager.notify(notificationId, builder.build());

        scheduleSnooze(notificationId, title, message);
    }

    private void scheduleSnooze(int notificationId, String title, String message) {
        Data inputData = new Data.Builder()
                .putInt("NOTIFICATION_ID", notificationId)
                .putString("TITLE", title)
                .putString("MESSAGE", message)
                .build();

        OneTimeWorkRequest workRequest = new OneTimeWorkRequest.Builder(SnoozeWorker.class)
                .setInitialDelay(5, TimeUnit.MINUTES)
                .setInputData(inputData)
                .build();

        WorkManager.getInstance(this).enqueue(workRequest);
    }
}
```

---

### 3. **Implement the Snooze Worker**
Create a `Worker` class for rescheduling notifications.

```java
public class SnoozeWorker extends Worker {

    public SnoozeWorker(@NonNull Context context, @NonNull WorkerParameters workerParams) {
        super(context, workerParams);
    }

    @NonNull
    @Override
    public Result doWork() {
        Context context = getApplicationContext();
        int notificationId = getInputData().getInt("NOTIFICATION_ID", -1);
        String title = getInputData().getString("TITLE");
        String message = getInputData().getString("MESSAGE");

        if (notificationId != -1) {
            NotificationManager notificationManager =
                    (NotificationManager) context.getSystemService(Context.NOTIFICATION_SERVICE);

            // Check if the notification is still active
            if (isNotificationActive(notificationManager, notificationId)) {
                // Re-issue the notification
                NotificationCompat.Builder builder = new NotificationCompat.Builder(context, "default_channel")
                        .setContentTitle(title)
                        .setContentText(message)
                        .setSmallIcon(R.drawable.ic_notification)
                        .setAutoCancel(true);

                NotificationManagerCompat.from(context).notify(notificationId, builder.build());

                // Reschedule snooze
                scheduleSnooze(notificationId, title, message);
            }
        }
        return Result.success();
    }

    private boolean isNotificationActive(NotificationManager notificationManager, int notificationId) {
        if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.M) {
            for (StatusBarNotification sbn : notificationManager.getActiveNotifications()) {
                if (sbn.getId() == notificationId) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    private void scheduleSnooze(int notificationId, String title, String message) {
        Data inputData = new Data.Builder()
                .putInt("NOTIFICATION_ID", notificationId)
                .putString("TITLE", title)
                .putString("MESSAGE", message)
                .build();

        OneTimeWorkRequest workRequest = new OneTimeWorkRequest.Builder(SnoozeWorker.class)
                .setInitialDelay(5, TimeUnit.MINUTES)
                .setInputData(inputData)
                .build();

        WorkManager.getInstance(getApplicationContext()).enqueue(workRequest);
    }
}
```

---

### 4. **Handle Notification Dismissal**
Use a `BroadcastReceiver` to listen for notification dismissal actions.

```java
public class NotificationDismissReceiver extends BroadcastReceiver {
    @Override
    public void onReceive(Context context, Intent intent) {
        if ("DISMISS".equals(intent.getAction())) {
            int notificationId = intent.getIntExtra("NOTIFICATION_ID", -1);
            if (notificationId != -1) {
                NotificationManager notificationManager =
                        (NotificationManager) context.getSystemService(Context.NOTIFICATION_SERVICE);
                notificationManager.cancel(notificationId);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 5. **Set Up Notification Channel**
Create a notification channel for Android 8.0+.

```java
public class App extends Application {
    @Override
    public void onCreate() {
        super.onCreate();
        createNotificationChannel();
    }

    private void createNotificationChannel() {
        if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.O) {
            NotificationChannel channel = new NotificationChannel(
                    "default_channel",
                    "Default Channel",
                    NotificationManager.IMPORTANCE_HIGH
            );
            NotificationManager manager = getSystemService(NotificationManager.class);
            if (manager != null) {
                manager.createNotificationChannel(channel);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 6. **Register Components in Manifest**
Update your `AndroidManifest.xml` to include the components.

```xml
<service
    android:name=".MyFirebaseMessagingService"
    android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
        <action android:name="com.google.firebase.MESSAGING_EVENT" />
    </intent-filter>
</service>

<receiver android:name=".NotificationDismissReceiver" />
```

